If a patient has a reproductive-potential then every clinician should discuss a future-pregnancy-intention with the patient.
If a patient has a reproductive-potential and some contraception is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should use a shared-decision-making with the patient for the contraception.
If a patient has a reproductive-potential and has a future-pregnancy-intention-discussion then the future-pregnancy-intention-discussion is a core-care-component.
If a patient has a reproductive-potential and some contraception is appropriate for the patient and the patient has a contraception-shared-decision-making then the contraception-shared-decision-making is a core-care-component.
